            "Using an irregular plural incorrectly (foots instead of feet)"
        ],
        "explanation": "Unit names such as second or foot may be written in the plural (seconds, feet) because tools apply a standard pluralizer. Unit symbols such as ms and Hz are abbreviations that already stand for singular and plural and take no s. Hertz is its own plural.",
        "correction_strategy": "Use the singular symbol, or the standard plural of the unit name",
        "correction_examples": [
            {
                "wrong": "Frequency/3 hertzs",
                "correct": "Frequency/3 hertz",
                "explanation": "Hertz is both singular and plural"
            },
            {
                "wrong": "Time-value/5 mss",
                "correct": "Time-value/5 ms",
                "explanation": "Symbols are never pluralized"
            },
            {
                "wrong": "Frequency/3 Hzs",
                "correct": "Frequency/3 Hz",
                "explanation": "Symbols are never pluralized"
            }
        ],
        "correction_patterns": [
            "Never pluralize a symbol",
            "Use the dictionary plural of a unit name",
            "When unsure, use the singular form"
        ],
        "fix_instructions": [
            "1. Check whether the unit is a symbol (short abbreviation such as ms, Hz, km) or a name (second, foot, hertz)",
            "2. For a symbol, remove any trailing s",
            "3. For a name, use its standard English plural or the singular"
        ],
        "validation_hints": [
